---
code: K0025
title: Placeholder Outside Call
severity: ERROR
since: 0.1.0
category: parse
deprecated: False
tags: [parse, syntax, wildcard, placeholder, pipe, partial-application]
description: "'_' placeholder is only allowed in pipe stages or as a whole call argument"
---

The `_` placeholder is only legal either inside the right-hand stage of a forward pipe (`x |> _ + 1` or `x |> f(g(_))`) or as a whole argument in a function call for partial application (`add(_, 10)`). It cannot be used as a standalone value or inside arbitrary expressions outside a pipe.

## Example

This error occurs when `_` appears inside an arithmetic, record, or indexing expression outside a `|>` pipe stage, or as part of a compound argument expression in a call:

```kura
let bad-expr = _ + 1

let bad-arg = compute(_ + 1, 10)
```

## Solution

Use `_` as a whole call argument for partial application, place the expression on the right side of a `|>` pipe, or write an explicit lambda `(x) => ...`:

```kura
let add-ten = add(_, 10)

let piped = 5 |> _ + 1

let mapped = (x) => compute(x + 1, 10)
```
